{# ── Chapter: FE Depth ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="fe-depth">
  <h2>The same rule, in the places it's easy to miss</h2>
  <div class="tone-junior">
    <p>
      This bug hides especially well because the input looks and works fine the entire time the page is loading — it's only the moment data actually arrives that anything goes wrong, and by then whoever's testing the form may have already moved their attention elsewhere.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-mid">
    <p>
      Checkboxes and radios need the identical treatment for <code>checked</code> (<code>checked={someBoolean ?? false}</code>), and mixing <code>defaultValue</code> and <code>value</code> on the same element is its own separate React warning — not the one this case covers, but it's an easy trap to reach for when patching this one and land in a different warning instead.
    </p>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-staff">
    <p>
      The more durable fix, when it's practical, is to not let "no data yet" and "empty string" be different states your component has to reason about at all — model loading as its own explicit UI state (a skeleton, a disabled field) rather than rendering the real form early with placeholder-shaped props. That sidesteps the undefined-value problem structurally instead of patching it with <code>?? ''</code> at every call site that touches async data.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

