{# ── Chapter: Takeaway ── #}
<section class="case-chapter" data-chapter="takeaway">
  <h2>Remember</h2>
  <div class="case-takeaway">
    <h3>Key takeaways</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <div class="tone-junior">An input can't switch from uncontrolled to controlled mid-life — if value starts as undefined and later becomes a string, React warns, and the field's contents can get silently overwritten.</div>
        <div class="tone-mid">Give value (and checked) a real, same-shaped default from the very first render — value={"{state ?? ''}"} or useState('') instead of a bare useState() — so the input is controlled from render one, not eventually.</div>
        <div class="tone-staff">The same invariant applies anywhere state can start undefined and later resolve — fetched data, localStorage, conditional props — and the more durable fix is modeling "not loaded yet" as its own explicit UI state rather than rendering the real form with placeholder-shaped props.</div>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
